/// Exposes a Swift class to QML.
///
/// Apply this macro to a class to make its properties and methods
/// available from QML.
/// When applied, the macro adds conformance to ``QObjectBuildable``
/// and automatically exposes eligible members of the class.
///
/// A property is exposed to QML if it:
/// - Is declared `public`.
/// - Is a stored instance property.
/// - Has an explicitly declared type that is supported by
/// ``QVariant``.
///
/// Eligible properties are automatically annotated with
/// ``QtTracked()`` and become available in QML.
///
/// A method is exposed to QML if it:
/// - Is declared `public`.
/// - Is an instance method.
/// - Has argument types supported by ``QMetaParamsList``.
/// - Returns `Void`, or a value conforming to ``QVariantSettable``.
///
/// Use ``QtIgnored()`` to exclude specific members from being
/// exposed.
@attached(member, names: arbitrary)
@attached(memberAttribute)
@attached(extension, conformances: QObjectBuildable)
public macro QtBridgeable() = #externalMacro(module: "QtBridgeMacros", type: "QtBridgeableMacro")

/// Exposes a property to QML and enables change tracking.
///
/// Use this macro to expose a property to QML. When the property's
/// value changes, the QML engine is notified automatically.
///
/// The macro is applied automatically to properties whose type
/// is explicitly declared and supported by ``QVariant``.
/// You can also apply this macro to properties with implicitly
/// inferred types, as long as the type is supported by ``QVariant``.
/// For properties whose type is a custom Swift class, you must
/// apply `@QtTracked` manually. The referenced type must also be
/// annotated with a ``QtBridgeable()`` macro:
///
/// ```swift
/// @QtBridgeable
/// public class Person {
///     public var name: String = ""
///     public var number: Int = 0
/// }
///
/// @QtBridgeable
/// public class Phonebook {
///     @QtTracked
///     public var people: Person = Person()
/// }
/// ```
///
/// `@QtTracked` enables change tracking by adding a `didSet`
/// observer to non-constant properties.
@attached(accessor, names: named(didSet))
public macro QtTracked() = #externalMacro(module: "QtBridgeMacros", type: "QtTrackedMacro")

/// Prevents a property or method from being exposed to QML.
///
/// Use this macro to exclude a member from being exposed to QML
/// and disable automatic change tracking. By default, properties
/// and methods that use supported types are exposed to QML.
/// Apply `@QtIgnored` to opt out of this behavior for a specific
/// member.
///
/// When applied, the annotated member is omitted from
/// code generated by ``QtBridgeable()``, even if it would
/// otherwise be eligible for export:
///
/// ```swift
/// @QtBridgeable
/// public class Model {
///     @QtIgnored
///     public var internalId: Int = 42
/// }
/// ```
@attached(peer)
public macro QtIgnored() = #externalMacro(module: "QtBridgeMacros", type: "QtIgnoredMacro")

/// Defines custom QML signals using function declarations.
///
/// This macro provides a way to define custom QML signals using
/// function declarations. Annotated functions must not provide
/// an implementation. Instead, the macro generates the required
/// body and connects the function to the QML engine.
///
/// Functions may declare parameters of a type supported by
/// ``QVariant``, which are forwarded to QML as signal
/// arguments.
///
/// Signals can be handled in QML using `Connections` with
/// `onSignalName()` handlers:
/// For example, the following code applies `QtSignal` macro to
/// the function definition making it a signal:
///
/// ```swift
/// @QtBridgeable
/// public class MyModel {
///     @QtSignal
///     func mySignalWithoutParams()
///
///     @QtSignal
///     func mySignalWithParams(num: Int)
///
///     func triggerSignals() {
///         mySignalWithoutParams()
///         mySignalWithParams(num: 42)
///     }
/// }
/// ```
///
/// Then, in QML:
///
/// ```qml
/// Button {
///     id: triggerButton
///     onClicked: MyModel.triggerSignals()
/// }
///
/// Connections {
///     target: MyModel
///     function onMySignalWithoutParams() {
///         console.log("Signal fired!");
///     }
///
///     function onMySignalWithParams(num) {
///         console.log("My number: ", num);
///     }
/// }
/// ```
@attached(body)
public macro QtSignal() = #externalMacro(module: "QtBridgeMacros", type: "QtSignalMacro")
